# Property Analysis Skill — environment variables
# Copy this file to .env (or set vars directly in your shell) and fill in.

# ────────────────────────────────────────────
# RentCast (market rent comp adapter)
# ────────────────────────────────────────────
# RENTCAST_MODE controls which data source the adapter uses:
#   live    — hit the real RentCast API (requires RENTCAST_API_KEY)
#   fixture — read canned JSON from scripts/property_analysis/rentcast_fixtures/
#             (used for demos and tests; output is clearly labeled FIXTURE)
#   off     — return None for every call (skip variance flag entirely)
#
# Default behavior if neither var is set:
#   - RENTCAST_API_KEY present -> mode is "live"
#   - otherwise               -> mode is "fixture"
#
# Cache namespaces are isolated by mode (rentcast_cache/live, rentcast_cache/fixture, etc.)
# so fixture data CANNOT be returned in live mode and vice versa.

# RENTCAST_API_KEY=your_key_here
# RENTCAST_MODE=live
